Z||000000||Vlad||05-08-2001||02:48 AM||||Hello guys,<P>I have a problem. I got a instrument cluster and side gauges off 86 GT for my 85 GT.<BR>As a first step I installed cluster. It was plug and play and everything went OK. <BR>Today, I did gauges and something is wrong.<BR>Well... I used a wiring diagram that I got here at PFF. However, I'm not sure I understood it right. :-(<P>What I did with wires is I spliced the wires leading to the side gauge into the main harness behind the tachometer. So what I got for each of five wires is the original setup PLUS third wire going to the side gauge. Sort of T connection for each of them.<BR>As a result, the voltmeter and oil pressure gauges are alive, but voltmeter shows less than 8 volt and the warning light on the side gauge is ON. Oil pressure seems to be OK, however, the oil pressure idiot light on the main cluster (yes, there is a bulb there) is glowing, but I can see it only from the back of the cluster.<P>Well....  Sorry for unclear explanation, but ANY help is highly appreciated. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||05-09-2001||08:58 PM||||Do a search.  batboy had a thread with a wiring diagram.  (Gotta find that thread myself.)<P>MM||||reg||1
